WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.396 --> 00:00:06.560
King Midas was a very kind man.

2
00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.143
He loved to listen to music and eat delicious food.

3
00:00:11.824 --> 00:00:13.765
He also loved strolling in his rose garden.

4
00:00:15.366 --> 00:00:18.609
One evening a satyr named Silenus got lost.

5
00:00:19.889 --> 00:00:23.352
He wandered into King Midas' rose garden and soon fell asleep.

6
00:00:25.473 --> 00:00:30.485
The next morning King Midas' gardener found the satyr in the garden and took him to the king.

7
00:00:33.206 --> 00:00:35.047
Silenus stood before King Midas.

8
00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:38.688
"Why were you sleeping in my rose garden?"

9
00:00:38.988 --> 00:00:39.609
asked the king.

10
00:00:41.029 --> 00:00:46.372
Silenus explained how he had gotten lost, and King Midas felt sorry for the creature.

11
00:00:46.392 --> 00:00:48.953
"I will not punish you.

12
00:00:49.273 --> 00:00:51.494
You may go in peace," he said.

13
00:00:52.755 --> 00:00:54.976
Silenus was very grateful to King Midas.

14
00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.002
Silenus was an old friend of Dionysus, the god of wine.

15
00:01:01.443 --> 00:01:03.185
Dionysus was very powerful.

16
00:01:04.446 --> 00:01:07.788
He listened as Silenus told him about the kind King Midas.

17
00:01:09.709 --> 00:01:13.192
After hearing the story, Dionysus went to see King Midas.

18
00:01:14.593 --> 00:01:16.734
He wanted to reward him with a special gift.

19
00:01:16.754 --> 00:01:19.676
"You were kind to my friend.

20
00:01:20.137 --> 00:01:21.718
So I will give you one wish.

21
00:01:22.158 --> 00:01:24.820
You may have whatever you want," said Dionysus.

22
00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:30.621
The king did not have to think for very long.

23
00:01:31.881 --> 00:01:33.221
He knew exactly what he wanted.

24
00:01:33.241 --> 00:01:37.143
"I wish that everything I touch will turn to gold!"

25
00:01:37.563 --> 00:01:38.643
said the excited king.

26
00:01:46.165 --> 00:01:47.986
Then he picked up a stone from the ground.

27
00:01:49.146 --> 00:01:51.767
King Midas stared at the gold stone in his hand.

28
00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:54.187
His wish had come true!

29
00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.408
King Midas touched the door.

30
00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:58.177
He touched the throne.

31
00:01:59.037 --> 00:02:00.638
He ran over and touched the table.

32
00:02:00.658 --> 00:02:03.080
"I'm rich!

33
00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:05.102
I'm the richest man in the world!"

34
00:02:05.522 --> 00:02:06.543
shouted the happy king.

35
00:02:07.543 --> 00:02:12.767
King Midas had fun turning his possessions into gold, but before long, he was hungry.

36
00:02:12.787 --> 00:02:15.168
"Bring me my dinner!"

37
00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:16.329
boomed the king.

38
00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.792
The servant brought in a large dish of chicken.

39
00:02:20.972 --> 00:02:24.575
But when Midas picked up the chicken and bit it, what happened?

40
00:02:25.536 --> 00:02:27.233
Ouch! It turned to gold!

41
00:02:29.494 --> 00:02:32.777
The king was so hungry, but everything he touched turned to gold.

42
00:02:34.498 --> 00:02:35.659
How could he eat gold?

43
00:02:36.419 --> 00:02:37.380
It was not possible.

44
00:02:38.581 --> 00:02:41.122
The frustrated and hungry king needed some fresh air.

45
00:02:42.443 --> 00:02:45.986
The rose garden was the only place where King Midas could find peace.

46
00:02:47.687 --> 00:02:49.789
He reached out to smell one of the roses.

47
00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:54.532
When he touched the rose, it turned into gold and fell to the ground.

48
00:02:56.336 --> 00:03:01.298
As the king tried to run away, he bumped into the bushes and turned them all into gold.

49
00:03:01.318 --> 00:03:04.218
"Oh, my beautiful roses!"

50
00:03:04.799 --> 00:03:05.499
cried the king.

51
00:03:06.839 --> 00:03:09.140
King Midas was not enjoying himself anymore.

52
00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.721
The king was getting tired and wanted to rest.

53
00:03:13.981 --> 00:03:17.302
He laid his head on his pillow, but it turned to gold as well.

54
00:03:17.322 --> 00:03:21.224
"Why? Why did I make this wish?"

55
00:03:21.764 --> 00:03:22.404
cried the king.

56
00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.661
King Midas was the richest man in the world.

57
00:03:28.061 --> 00:03:31.542
He got exactly what he asked for: everything he touched turned to gold.

58
00:03:32.883 --> 00:03:33.823
But he was not happy.

59
00:03:34.843 --> 00:03:36.304
In fact, he was miserable.

60
00:03:37.964 --> 00:03:40.745
He could not eat, sleep, or admire his flowers.

61
00:03:42.425 --> 00:03:44.446
Then King Midas heard the royal trumpets.

62
00:03:45.666 --> 00:03:46.407
"At last!"

63
00:03:46.747 --> 00:03:47.447
shouted the king.

64
00:03:47.467 --> 00:03:50.968
"Here is someone who can make me happy again!"

65
00:03:53.301 --> 00:03:56.303
The king ran and opened the gold door to welcome his daughter.

66
00:03:57.545 --> 00:03:59.326
She had just returned from a long journey.

67
00:03:59.346 --> 00:04:03.791
"Father!" the princess shouted happily.

68
00:04:03.811 --> 00:04:05.613
"My daughter!"

69
00:04:05.873 --> 00:04:06.573
shouted the king.

70
00:04:07.855 --> 00:04:12.099
But as soon as King Midas touched the princess, she turned into a gold statue.

71
00:04:12.119 --> 00:04:14.862
"No! No!

72
00:04:15.362 --> 00:04:16.063
This must end!"

73
00:04:16.383 --> 00:04:16.964
cried the king.

74
00:04:19.996 --> 00:04:22.938
That evening Dionysus received an unexpected visit.

75
00:04:22.958 --> 00:04:28.562
"Please, I don't want the golden touch anymore," King Midas said sadly.

76
00:04:29.923 --> 00:04:32.585
"I thought you wanted to be rich," said Dionysus.

77
00:04:33.485 --> 00:04:36.407
"No amount of gold is worth losing the things I love."

78
00:04:37.848 --> 00:04:39.710
Dionysus felt sorry for Midas.

79
00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:43.992
"I wish I had never asked for this gift," Midas said.

80
00:04:44.012 --> 00:04:48.896
"I'm glad you learned a lesson from this," Dionysus told the king.

81
00:04:49.728 --> 00:04:51.249
"I will grant you your new wish."

82
00:04:52.090 --> 00:04:54.472
Everything the king had touched returned to normal.

83
00:04:56.454 --> 00:04:59.336
King Midas was so happy to have all his things restored.

84
00:05:01.117 --> 00:05:03.640
Most of all, he was happy to have his daughter back.

85
00:05:05.001 --> 00:05:08.323
King Midas was not as rich as before, but it didn't matter.

86
00:05:09.725 --> 00:05:13.287
For he learned that the best things in life are not made of gold.
